<mxCell id="c203" value="$$(E, \tau=0, \rho=0)$$" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=20;fontFamily=Helvetica;" parent="1" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="-75.0" y="-330.0" width="240.0" height="34.0" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
<mxCell id="c204" value="&lt;b&gt;Definitions.&lt;/b&gt; A transition without a box has guard None and reward r = 0.&lt;br&gt;new(): a fresh case. Claims and complaints: risk ~ U{0,1,2}, bad ~ Bernoulli(p&lt;sub&gt;risk&lt;/sub&gt;) with p = (0.1, 0.5, 0.9), and reworked = 0 for complaints; bad is not observable. Underwriting: task_type ~ U{0,1}.&lt;br&gt;d&lt;sub&gt;f&lt;/sub&gt; = 1 + U{0,1} (approve, resolve); d&lt;sub&gt;s&lt;/sub&gt;(Y) = 4 + U{0,1} for a normal clerk (skill = 0) and 2 + U{0,1} for an expert (skill = 1) (investigate, check).&lt;br&gt;d(X,Y) = 1 + U{0,1} if X.task_type = Y.code, else 3 + U{0,1}.&lt;br&gt;X' = X with reworked = 1 and bad = 0: a wrongly resolved complaint reopens after 2 time units.&lt;br&gt;S: an employee of the staff pool. To claims or complaints, it joins the clerks with its skill (expert: skill = 1); to underwriting, it becomes an underwriter for task type c ({code=c})." style="text;strokeColor=#666666;fillColor=#ffffff;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=7;spacingRight=7;spacingTop=4;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=14;fontFamily=Helvetica;" parent="1" vertex="1"><mxGeometry x="-70.0" y="886.0" width="1468.7" height="141.4" as="geometry" /></mxCell>
</root></mxGraphModel></diagram></mxfile>